# SLIC

A MATLAB toolbox for groupwise whole-brain parcellation of resting-state fMRI data.

[GPL-3.0 license](LICENSE) · [Technical notes](Readme_plus)

The toolbox includes five methods: MSC mean, MSC two-level, MKSC, SLIC mean, and SLIC two-level. The original documentation identifies [SLIC_2](https://github.com/yuzhounh/SLIC_2) as an updated version.

## Quick Start

1. Prepare MATLAB with Parallel Computing Toolbox and the NIfTI tools used by the scripts.
2. Obtain the preprocessed demo data linked in the [NITRC downloads](https://www.nitrc.org/frs/?group_id=1030), and extract subject images under `data/` using the expected `subNNNNN` naming convention.
3. Review [Readme_plus](Readme_plus) for the original 40-subject experiment, preprocessing, software versions, and memory requirements. Adjust worker counts in [main_algorithm.m](main_algorithm.m) for your machine.
4. Run from the repository directory:

```matlab
main_parc
```

[main_toolbox.m](main_toolbox.m) attempts to download and extract `NIfTI_20140122.zip`. The historical download endpoint and the full experiment have not been revalidated in a current environment.

## Repository Structure

- [main_parc.m](main_parc.m): preparation, parcellation, evaluation, and plotting.
- [main_subject.m](main_subject.m): discovers subject files under `data/`.
- [main_algorithm.m](main_algorithm.m): runs the parcellation methods.
- [main_eval.m](main_eval.m) and [main_plot.m](main_plot.m): evaluation and result plots.
- [graymatter.nii](graymatter.nii) and [T1_4mm.nii](T1_4mm.nii): image resources.
- [Readme_plus](Readme_plus): detailed experimental notes.

## Citation

Jing Wang and Haixian Wang. *A supervoxel-based method for groupwise whole brain parcellation with resting-state fMRI data.* Frontiers in Human Neuroscience. [doi:10.3389/fnhum.2016.00659](https://doi.org/10.3389/fnhum.2016.00659).

